.Dd August 1, 2026
.Dt INTEGRISD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm integrisd
.Nd privilege-separated filesystem sync and backup daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the intended product daemon for Integris: a privilege-separated service that
synchronizes and backs up explicitly authorized filesystem archives between
mutually authenticated nodes on macOS,
.Fx ,
Linux, and
.Ox .
.Pp
.Sy Status :
an engineering preview binary exists for
.Cm serve
.Pq M2a Ns – Ns M4p :
privilege-separated eight-role receive chain —
.Nm Ns -auth ,
.Nm Ns -parser ,
.Nm Ns -plan ,
.Nm Ns -index
(readonly destination scan),
.Nm Ns -apply
(openat staging and publish on conferred allow-root FDs),
.Nm Ns -journal
(openat bootstrap and reopen on conferred allow-root FDs),
.Nm Ns -audit
(openat sink bootstrap on conferred allow-root FDs),
and
.Nm Ns -net
over local IPC.
Optional per-peer PSK allow-list
.Pq Fl peer-key
is held by
.Nm Ns -auth
.Pq M2i .
Optional
.Fl strict-launch
selects fail-closed release-shaped launch
.Pq M2k ,
including FreeBSD CapEnter self-check
.Pq M3m ,
Capsicum rights-limit checks
.Pq M3n Ns / Ns M3o ,
ambient FS-read deny
.Pq M3q ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter RestartOne first cut
.Pq M3r ,
FreeBSD ambient AF_INET residual documentation
.Pq M3s ,
and FreeBSD sealed MAC key FD
.Pq M3t ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter parser-down RestartOne
.Pq M3u ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter auth-primary RestartOne
.Pq M3v ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter M2j auth ExtraPeer RestartOne
.Pq M3w ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter M2j audit ExtraPeer RestartOne
.Pq M3x ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter M2j peer-key push
.Pq M3y ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter M2j apply RestartOne
.Pq M3z ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter M2j parser-down RestartOne
.Pq M4a ,
and FreeBSD CapEnter M2j peer deny/admit
.Pq M4b ,
and Darwin/OpenBSD anon key FD residual documentation
.Pq M4c ,
and non-FreeBSD release ambient ROLE-NET deny
.Pq M4d ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt push first cut
.Pq M4e ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt RestartOne apply
.Pq M4f ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt parser-down RestartOne
.Pq M4g ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt auth-primary RestartOne
.Pq M4h ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt auth ExtraPeer RestartOne
.Pq M4i ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt audit ExtraPeer RestartOne
.Pq M4j ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt peer-key Once push
.Pq M4k ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt peer deny/admit
.Pq M4l ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt peer apply RestartOne
.Pq M4m ,
and Darwin StrictLaunch Seatbelt peer parser-down RestartOne
.Pq M4n ,
and Linux StrictLaunch Landlock+seccomp push first cut
.Pq M4o ,
and Linux StrictLaunch Landlock+seccomp RestartOne apply
.Pq M4p .
Default key conferral is SCM-only on a dedicated key channel
.Pq M2l .
It is not the release product daemon, not PKI, and not the full nine-role
model.
See
.Pa docs/daemon-m2a.md .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
integrisd serve -destination DIR -key HEX|-keyfile PATH \\
  [-addr HOST:PORT] [-once] [-max-restarts N]
integrisd serve -destination DIR -peer-key ID=PATH... \\
  [-addr HOST:PORT] [-once] [-max-restarts N]
.Ed
.Pp
.Fl peer-key
is repeatable and mutually exclusive with
.Fl key
/
.Fl keyfile .
Without
.Fl once ,
the supervisor accepts multiple pushes and may restart the role set after
an unexpected child exit
.Pq Fl max-restarts .
.Ss Process model
The architecture separates authority across supervised roles
(see
.Pa docs/security-architecture.md ) :
.Bl -tag -width "integrisd-supervisor" -compact
.It integrisd-supervisor
Child lifecycle, pre-opened IPC, policy identity.
.It integrisd-net
Bounded encrypted network frames.
.It integrisd-auth
Identity, session keys, authorization policy.
.It integrisd-parser
Bounded message parse/serialize over IPC.
.It integrisd-index
Read-only archive indexing.
.It integrisd-plan
Deterministic planning.
.It integrisd-apply
Descriptor-relative archive mutation.
.It integrisd-journal
Append-only authenticated journal.
.It integrisd-audit
Redacted event sink.
.El
.Pp
Operators configure archives, peers, and policy; the daemon plans, transfers,
journals, and recovers under least authority.
Native platform facilities required by INT-IC4-0001 must be preferred on each
declared OS.
.Ss Configuration
A future release will load an immutable, versioned configuration document.
Today, configuration documents may be validated without side effects using
.Xr integris-verify-config 1 .
.Ss Service integration
When packaged, installations should register
.Nm
with the host service manager (for example launchd on macOS, rc or service
scripts on
.Fx
and
.Ox ,
or service units on Linux) using a dedicated account and the confinement
composition in
.Pa docs/platform-matrix.md .
Missing required confinement must refuse startup for release modes.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/integris/config.json" -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/integris/
Typical configuration directory for a
.Pa /usr/local
prefix install (layout may vary by package).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Reserved for clean shutdown after a successful run (when shipped).
.It 1
Operational failure or refused startup.
.It 2
Usage or configuration error.
.El
.Pp
In this baseline, any accidental
.Nm
binary that is not a signed release artifact should exit non-zero.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Validate configuration before any daemon exists:
integris-verify-config -config /usr/local/etc/integris/config.json

# After a future release package is installed (examples):
# service integrisd start           # FreeBSD
# rcctl enable integrisd            # OpenBSD
# systemctl enable --now integrisd  # Linux
# launchctl bootstrap system ...    # macOS
.Ed
